econstruction-dark-era-crossover?p=1067069#post1067069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haven't got that far yet, but I'm getting there! The dates were interesting, it was earlier than I expected. Overlaps directly with the end of Blood Flows West from Vampire, which is cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't have any role in setting the dates. <br /> <br /> Fun fact, if you're curious, there are some historians who advocate for dropping &quot;The Gilded Age&quot; and instead talking about extended Reconstruction and Progressive Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:49:04-07:00","id":1067186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1051744-reconstruction-dark-era-crossover?p=1067132#post1067132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact, if you're curious, there are some historians who advocate for dropping &quot;The Gilded Age&quot; and instead talking about extended Reconstruction and Progressive Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>But &quot;Gilded Age&quot; so perfectly encapsulates an edifice of post-war unity, industrial progress, and patriotic revival that conceals a reality of unhealed festering wounds, burgeoning inequality, and political corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:07:38-07:00","id":1067198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1051744-reconstruction-dark-era-crossover?p=1067186#post1067186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But &quot;Gilded Age&quot; so perfectly encapsulates an edifice of post-war unity, industrial progress, and patriotic revival that conceals a reality of unhealed festering wounds, burgeoning inequality, and political corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately, humans have never really understood satire.<br /> <br /> Still, I have to say-I like the stark catharsis the authors took towards Reconstruction. The bad peace more or less made the entire damn Civil War nearly pointless, and all anyone was left with was a lot of heartache and bad memories. <br /> <br /> I also love how one of the Heroes is actually a John Brown-esque anti-racist militant. Just because the cause is just...although I suspect he's one of those Heroes you can talk down (&quot;Wait, ye lads only menace the KKK? ...I believe I've made a terrible mistake.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:26:15-07:00","id":1067385,"title":"","content":"I've come to the point of viewing Reconstruction in the continuum of American projects in occupation and nation-building. Early attempts at transformative change stymied by attendant instability, local resistance, insurgent terrorism, and a lack of political will. Ultimately followed by a reverse course, support for a regressive but more stable regime with a new coat of paint, and an exit that allows for a declaration of victory without many real achieved objectives. Then the entire enterprise is mostly relegated to the back room of popular memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:56:38-07:00","id":1067421,"title":"","content":"Took me a while for the opening intro to &quot;click&quot;, but once I read through the historical background it made more sense. I'm very impressed by how effectively you stuck with your guns at calling the Reconstruction &quot;Post-Apocolyptic&quot; and then showing just how accurate that descriptor was. I would not have thought it possible, but clearly I was wrong.<br /> <br /> The continuity of the Mage section seems a bit weird. The connection to the Nameless War is apt, but the text seems to suggest that the Nameless War and Civil War end at similar times, when the Nameless War continues for another 35 years and doesn't finish until the dawn of the 20th Century. Likewise, the references to the Free Council also seem out of place to me, since they don't exist until properly until the literal last day of the 19th century. Now, if the intent is for that crossover to refer to the South in the early 20th century, that may be on me for reading comprehension, I'm up reading much later than I should be.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you for calling the KKK terrorists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T00:06:44-07:00","id":1067430,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>, shhhh....the Invisible Masters might hear that you too were uneffected by the Rite....<br /> <br /> *caughtchangesubject*<br /> <br /> Excellent work on the Reconstruction chapter. I especially love the NPCs (both Begotten, Heroes, and other lovelies) and the Reconstruction Era Nightmares. It might be a long shot, but I'd love to see another Beast Dark Era setting for World War I.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:04:25-07:00","id":1067554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1051744-reconstruction-dark-era-crossover?p=1067421#post1067421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The continuity of the Mage section seems a bit weird. The connection to the Nameless War is apt, but the text seems to suggest that the Nameless War and Civil War end at similar times, when the Nameless War continues for another 35 years and doesn't finish until the dawn of the 20th Century. Likewise, the references to the Free Council also seem out of place to me, since they don't exist until properly until the literal last day of the 19th century. Now, if the intent is for that crossover to refer to the South in the early 20th century, that may be on me for reading comprehension, I'm up reading much later than I should be.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you for calling the KKK terrorists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rachel and I will always and forever call the KKK terrorists.<br /> <br /> Re: the Mage section, I think the first peripheral issue to this is the dates put down for the Era, which are not what I think they ought to be. But additionally, you may have noticed that for both this Era and A Grimm Dark Era, I project forward or look back when needed to provide context. I reference World War I in both Eras! And in other places in this chapter, the context I'm giving you is back to the seventeenth century. My concern is primarily with providing the context and foresight needed to understand not only where you are in the Era, but how you got there and where you may be going. And when an event starts at the same time as the Era itself, I can't control when it ended =P. I hope that makes sense. I'm concerned with giving you a picture of the Long Reconstruction, as well as the effects of different events and what caused them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:07:44-07:00","id":1067556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1051744-reconstruction-dark-era-crossover?p=1067430#post1067430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;4433&quot;]Excellent work on the Reconstruction chapter. I especially love the NPCs (both Begotten, Heroes, and other lovelies) and the Reconstruction Era Nightmares. It might be a long shot, but I'd love to see another Beast Dark Era setting for World War I.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Matt asked me what I thought the Beast Dark Era should be, I suggested WWI. I'd love to see it too.<br /> <br /> And thanks!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","n